Smart Hospital Queue Solution App

The Docs folder contains all the research and planning work carried out during the Design
Thinking process. This includes a comprehensive understanding of user needs, behaviors, and
challenges in hospital waiting environments.

The complete documentation, covering user research, empathy mapping, 10+ detailed
personas, insights, and problem definition, has been prepared and organized using Canva.

As part of the Empathize and Define stage, user data was collected through surveys and
analyzed to identify key pain points such as long waiting times, anxiety, lack of engagement,
and uncertainty. Based on these insights, detailed empathy maps were created to represent
what users think, feel, see, hear, and do during their waiting experience.

Additionally, more than 10 user personas were developed to reflect a diverse group of
patients, including elderly individuals, children, first-time visitors, and patients with chronic
conditions. These personas helped in understanding different user perspectives and guided
the design decisions.

A clear and focused problem statement was then defined using the insights gathered,
ensuring that the solution directly addresses real-world user needs.
All documentation has been carefully organized and designed using Canva for clarity and
visual presentation.

